WEBVTT

00:34:28.278 --> 00:34:32.821
and I think these ideas could
help us achieve these objectives

00:34:32.845 --> 00:34:34.436
more effectively."

00:34:34.460 --> 00:34:36.496
And I think you need to start there.

00:34:36.520 --> 00:34:39.610
AG: She realized there was another part
of her authentic identity

00:34:39.634 --> 00:34:41.226
that she could express.

00:34:41.250 --> 00:34:44.186
She wasn't just a heretic
who saw problems.

00:34:44.210 --> 00:34:46.286
She was also someone who solved them.

00:34:46.310 --> 00:34:48.746
CM: I would describe myself
as a change agent.

00:34:48.770 --> 00:34:50.046
I use that word.

00:34:50.070 --> 00:34:53.286
AG: Carmen had set herself up
to have real influence.

00:34:53.310 --> 00:34:55.956
After September 11, 2001,

00:34:55.980 --> 00:34:58.266
her colleagues were
finally forced to recognize

00:34:58.290 --> 00:35:01.019
the importance of speed
in sharing information.